WEBVTT

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.270
Everyone came back to the Nadesico.

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:09.760
They all came to realize that this was their place to be.

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:13.430
We should have known that from the beginning,

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.780
but instead we had to think about it long and hard.

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:18.880
Definitely BAKA-bakka.

00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:01.100
Ubiquitous "Righteousness"

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:03.520
I wonder if this was right.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:05.780
Listen to yourself, Yurika!

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:08.330
Aren't we going to end this war through negotiation?

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:11.120
That's right. We'll request that each side shoulder some blame.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:12.440
You don't think that's adequate?

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:14.550
No, you're right about that.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.510
But now that I'm out here, I got to thinking some more.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:20.450
About the people that were killed by the Lizard-san, for instance.

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:21.620
And other things as well...

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:24.290
Do you think our choice was wrong?

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:27.460
Would we be better off the way we were on Earth?

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:34.540
Of course not, but I don't have the confidence within myself to say that what I'm doing now is right.

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:36.420
I believe in myself.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:41.720
I believe in myself, and him.

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:46.060
Why do you stop me, Genichirou?!

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:50.860
If you were to leave solely to be a scout for peace, then I would not stop you.

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:51.770
However...

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:59.690
I never imagined you would fall prey to an Earth woman.

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:01.980
I thought the ideal woman for us was this!

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:03.910
Nanako-san, right here!

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:08.380
Nanako-san is a wonderful woman,

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:09.330
but...

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:11.130
But what?

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:14.050
She only exist in 2D world!

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:20.100
Tsukumo!

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:27.020
Detecting a boson jump directly ahead.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.820
Enemy Gekigan type confirmed.

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:35.490
Anti-Earth Cooperative Federation of the Jovian Realm of Ganymede, Callisto, and Europa,

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:37.740
Lieutenant Commander in the Space Assault Yuujin Forces,

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.410
Shiratori Tsukumo, here to work with you.

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:42.070
Thank you for coming.

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:46.590
Onii-chan...

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.060
Onii-chan...

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:52.890
ONII-CHAN!

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:55.920
Yukina, how are you doing?

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:03.050
Would you mind telling me your name this time?

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:08.070
Tenkawa Akito. I'm a pilot and a cook.

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:10.480
There is something that I would like to show you.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:11.730
For me?

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:15.550
Special edited selection, Intense Fight Volume?

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:19.400
A video tape in this day and age...

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:23.320
If it wasn't for my collection of obsolete decks, you wouldn't have been able to watch this.

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:25.240
Just remember that.

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:26.520
Yes, yes.

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:31.390
Why do I have to put up with this?

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:33.730
What can you do? He's an important guest.

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:35.990
The whole crew has to chip in to make this special.

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:41.740
All right then, switch on!

00:04:57.430 --> 00:05:02.660
yume ga asu wo yondeiru tamashii no sakebi sa

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:03.170
RETTSU GOO PASSHON...

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:03.650
Hmm, Ba...!

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:04.050
BAKA-bakka!

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:04.120
RETTSU GOO PASSHON...

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:05.080
BAKA-bakka!

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:08.450
Grownups should know better than to watch a cartoon like that.

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:10.250
It's so unnatural!

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:12.200
What?

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:14.210
Nothing.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.930
Akito, I understand now.

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:26.700
Gekiganger is the answer!

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:30.970
Who understands a group that loves justice and righteousness like us?

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:37.060
It's not the UEAF nor Nergal, but the Jovian Lizards-san!

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:40.820
Because the Jovian Lizards-san love Gekiganger!

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:42.590
Hey, just a second here...

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:43.740
That's right!

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:48.160
Love, courage, and passion will bring about peace to this world.

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:52.830
Gekiganger teaches us the true beauty of humanity!

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:56.070
I'm ashamed of myself!

00:05:56.420 --> 00:05:58.680
I made fun of this show as children's programming,

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:00.000
but I was wrong!

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:02.840
I've been in the industry, and I can't recall recent works

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:04.930
where the producers' sincerity shines through this clearly.

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:07.840
It's a work that deserves to be praised more.

00:06:08.230 --> 00:06:11.260
This is no simple anime. It's a wonderful story of human drama.

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:13.980
That's right. The path that we needed to take

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:15.960
is in fact Gekiganger!

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:20.110
I didn't realize that.

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:23.990
I want to know more, more about Gekiganger!

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:25.600
You want models, I got models!

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:27.350
And here are the production model sheets!

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:31.580
This isn't enough! I want to know a lot, a lot, a lot more!

00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:49.830
Hikaru-chan, please look this way!

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:50.600
Sure!

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:52.510
1 /8th scale Aquamarine!

00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:55.180
Only fifty limited edition models available!

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:57.600
Behold the skill of the casting magician!

00:06:57.870 --> 00:06:59.520
Go, go, go!

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:02.530
Listen to me closely, foolish Earthlings.

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:05.440
This hall has been taken over by the Dark String Universe!

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:08.240
Oh, not that easily!

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:10.360
Come on, everyone, let's fight on behalf of peace!

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:11.280
Let's...

00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:14.000
Gekiga-in!

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:17.220
And so we've finally started this presentation.

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:19.170
Yes, here we go.

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:21.510
As the main event featured in this Gekiganger Festival,

00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:23.030
this screening will show...

00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:27.130
Every episode of Gekiganger, starting from the first to the last episode of the series.

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:36.670
If he were alive, Gai sure would be happy right about now.

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:40.550
Hey, Akito, what happens at the end of Gekiganger?

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:44.200
Well, in most super robot anime, the series has a happy ending.

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:47.060
I see. A happy ending.

00:07:47.390 --> 00:07:48.980
Yes, that would be great!

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:52.450
But actually, I don't know.

00:07:53.960 --> 00:07:56.290
I've never watched the last episode.

00:07:56.850 --> 00:07:58.610
You're kidding. Why not?

00:07:59.190 --> 00:08:02.900
I had this fear that once I saw the last episode of Gekiganger,

00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:04.180
it would also end inside myself.

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:07.290
But I'm going to watch it this time.

00:08:07.730 --> 00:08:12.010
I want to see the last episode with everyone and make peace with Jupiter a reality.

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:18.100
Let's go, Gekiganger 3.

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:21.950
Got it?

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:23.590
Not yet.

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:26.560
I don't mind people touching it, but...

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:28.580
Maybe we should keep it attached with string.

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:30.430
That's after we have found it.

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:33.740
No one's here.

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:38.030
Now we can finally be alone together.

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:43.580
Could you, would you mind stepping back?

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:45.000
No.

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:51.580
Please! I'm not used to situations like this.

00:08:52.610 --> 00:08:53.970
You're so cute!

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:58.930
In our world, we rarely have the opportunity to come in contact with women.

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:01.850
So, you've never kissed someone?

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:03.770
Right.

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:06.280
Would you like me to teach you?

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:07.950
But that's...

00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:09.580
You don't want to?

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:11.260
Oh, well...

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:12.110
Make up your mind!

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:13.780
I'm not against it.

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:15.950
Then I shall teach you.

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:17.450
Close your eyes.

00:09:18.110 --> 00:09:18.760
Yes.

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:20.940
Tip your head forward.

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:22.370
Like this?

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:25.740
Yes, and put your arms here and here.

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:26.470
Yes.

00:09:26.470 --> 00:09:27.790
Don't open your eyes.

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:29.380
I'm sorry.

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:33.330
Don't move now. Is your heart pounding?

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:34.090
Yes.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:35.810
Same here.

00:09:43.610 --> 00:09:44.770
How did that feel?

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:11.460
What's wrong?

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:14.340
This is my room.

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:18.200
Oh yeah, right. Later!

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:18.830
Akito...

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:26.640
Akito, you said before, you'd watch the last episode of Gekiganger.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:31.440
Would you mind making a big decision, regarding me?

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:41.090
Stare...

00:10:41.890 --> 00:10:42.730
Gaze...

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:46.790
What's up, Yukina-chan?

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:50.830
I'm looking for onii-chan. He hasn't come back to our room.

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:53.060
Oh, Shiratori-san's in the mess hall.

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:53.830
Ah, Baka!

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:56.270
Mess hall, right. Stride, stride...

00:10:56.270 --> 00:10:57.670
Not now!

00:10:57.670 --> 00:11:00.030
Oh, I just remembered. You should wait a little longer.

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:01.220
Why is that?

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:03.780
Hey, onii-chan!

00:11:04.340 --> 00:11:05.160
Yo!

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:10.770
Continue in part B.

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:19.750
We've finally found it?!

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:23.660
Yes, we finally have the city within our grasp.

00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:29.950
Not only can we replenish our supply of artifacts from the ancient solar system civilization,

00:11:30.770 --> 00:11:34.410
but the war against Earth will take on a different meaning.

00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:37.340
What of the peace talks with Earth?

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:40.760
It's under debate in the Jovian Federation Supreme War Council.

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:47.180
This will probably be used effectively as ammunition to push back the supporters of a peace settlement.

00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:50.780
I will participate in the peace talks as well.

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:55.020
And I have a special assignment for you.

00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:56.940
Special assignment?

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:00.790
Tomorrow's going to be the last day of Geki-Fes.

00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:02.680
I'll miss it when it's over.

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:05.800
But Gekiganger doesn't end here.

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:10.260
I see the peace talks as a different form of Gekiganger.

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:12.820
I agree with that opinion.

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.210
All hearts that long for peace beat alike.

00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:21.830
I plan on proposing to a certain person once Geki-Fes is over.

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:25.930
Have you thought about what you plan to do when the war's over?

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:28.580
I haven't thought that far into the future.

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:31.990
I plan on starting a family with the woman I love.

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:33.940
You don't hesitate at all when you say that.

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:36.480
A day like that will come for you as well.

00:12:37.460 --> 00:12:39.550
Once you've encountered your true love,

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:42.630
you won't hesitate in making decisions,

00:12:42.630 --> 00:12:44.710
no matter how agonizing the circumstances.

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:48.730
Your true love...

00:12:56.010 --> 00:12:57.750
We're at the last episode, Akito.

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:10.600
Super Decisive Battle
Genkiganger Forever

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:13.680
Emergency alert. Jovian fleet approaching.

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:18.660
Incoming message from enemy vessel.

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:20.190
Patch it through, please.

00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:23.110
I am Vice Admiral Kusakabe, the Jovian Federation representative.

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:26.030
I am Misumaru Yurika, captain of the Nadesico.

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:31.080
In anticipation of starting the talks as soon as possible, we have come forward.

00:13:31.390 --> 00:13:32.370
I see.

00:13:32.670 --> 00:13:34.670
I would like to start talks in one hour.

00:13:35.110 --> 00:13:36.710
We will inform you of details later.

00:13:37.350 --> 00:13:39.720
Understood. Until later, then.

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:52.160
This is sooner than we expected, but here we go with the peace negotiations.

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:53.960
I'm sure this will work out.

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:55.810
After all, Shiratori-san will be acting as a go-between.

00:13:56.440 --> 00:13:58.110
Yes, but we should not let our guard down.

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:00.020
Is that jealousy?

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:02.450
I don't mix business with pleasure.

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:04.500
Is that the case?

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:08.570
So, you wouldn't tell your girlfriend to get off the ship?

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:10.870
The past is the past. Now is something else.

00:14:11.420 --> 00:14:13.790
I don't feel comfortable here.

00:14:17.420 --> 00:14:19.030
And so it starts.

00:14:19.030 --> 00:14:19.690
Yes.

00:14:19.690 --> 00:14:21.170
You make me proud, onii-chan.

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:38.350
What is all this about?

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:43.280
Some paperwork we prepared in hope of expediting the talks.

00:14:43.590 --> 00:14:46.570
No, it isn't. There is nothing conciliatory in this!

00:14:47.270 --> 00:14:48.750
The disarming of the Earth and surrounding space.

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:49.960
The breakup of financial conglomerates.

00:14:49.960 --> 00:14:51.510
Conversion of political ideologies.

00:14:51.510 --> 00:14:53.330
Do you intend to make Earth your colony?

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:55.500
Are these the conditions for peace?

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:56.850
They are.

00:14:57.260 --> 00:14:58.520
This can't be.

00:14:59.270 --> 00:15:01.000
I request the withdrawal of these papers.

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:02.420
Shiratori...

00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:04.880
State your reason, Lieutenant Commander Shiratori.

00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:05.980
The reason is...

00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:10.010
Because they too love Gekiganger. That is the reason.

00:15:11.120 --> 00:15:11.930
Shiratori-san...

00:15:12.190 --> 00:15:16.230
When I arrived here, I watched Gekiganger all over again.

00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:18.140
It's a wonderful manga.

00:15:18.550 --> 00:15:21.860
Vigilance, victory, friendship, and love!

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:26.650
That work embodies all ideals which are important to all people.

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:29.860
They have come forward to sue for peace upon this realization.

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:32.950
There must be only one true righteous path!

00:15:33.890 --> 00:15:37.240
Yes, as you say, there is only one true righteous path.

00:15:49.100 --> 00:15:50.260
Shiratori-san!

00:15:55.090 --> 00:15:56.220
My leg fell asleep.

00:15:58.260 --> 00:16:00.650
Why?! Why did you shoot him?!

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:05.570
The evil empire is destroyed by righteousness.

00:16:06.010 --> 00:16:08.240
That's the ending of Gekiganger.

00:16:09.640 --> 00:16:11.610
The evil empire deserves to be destroyed.

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:14.600
That is the central theme of the series.

00:16:15.090 --> 00:16:20.000
In other words, Earth, the oppressors who banished us to Jupiter, deserves to be destroyed!

00:16:20.590 --> 00:16:21.290
No!

00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:23.920
Are you telling me that we are the evil empire?!

00:16:24.430 --> 00:16:27.010
Exactly! There is only one true righteous path.

00:16:27.010 --> 00:16:28.090
Our path!

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:30.500
I don't care about any of that!

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:32.190
Help him!

00:16:32.190 --> 00:16:33.800
Help Shiratori-san!

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:35.890
Tenkawa!

00:16:38.460 --> 00:16:39.640
Damn it all!

00:16:45.320 --> 00:16:48.570
They suddenly attacked us. What's going on?

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:49.940
Forget that, where's Tenkawa and the others?!

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:51.100
Hurry!

00:16:59.710 --> 00:17:02.040
Can you pull back far enough to get out of their range?

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:04.960
That would entail abandoning the Hinagiku.

00:17:08.320 --> 00:17:09.090
Moderate damage to engineering.

00:17:10.570 --> 00:17:12.180
We will no longer be able to continue evasive action.

00:17:14.790 --> 00:17:15.390
Yurika...

00:17:20.830 --> 00:17:21.890
It's Akito-kun and the others!

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:23.520
Okay, here we go!

00:17:27.530 --> 00:17:28.600
Onii-chan!

00:17:28.600 --> 00:17:29.570
Cover the Hinagiku!

00:17:34.640 --> 00:17:35.530
It's the end.

00:17:39.900 --> 00:17:40.400
Damn!

00:17:53.110 --> 00:17:54.780
Didn't I tell you guys?

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:57.090
What the hell are you doing?

00:17:58.360 --> 00:18:00.310
You've come to help us?

00:18:00.310 --> 00:18:02.030
What choice do I have with this going on?

00:18:02.300 --> 00:18:04.580
Get out of there while we cover you.

00:18:08.410 --> 00:18:10.110
Onii-chan! Onii-chan!

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:13.280
Right, get it ready! At least the anesthetic!

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:17.470
Onii-chan! Onii-chan! Onii-chan! Onii-chan!

00:18:18.790 --> 00:18:20.280
Can we fire the phase transition cannon?

00:18:20.970 --> 00:18:21.890
Captain!

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:25.080
If you use that now, all hopes for a peaceful settlement will die...

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:25.810
That's fine.

00:18:26.170 --> 00:18:27.120
Are you sure?

00:18:27.980 --> 00:18:29.250
Are you absolutely sure?

00:18:31.180 --> 00:18:33.050
Retrieving Aestivalis units.

00:18:35.850 --> 00:18:36.510
Onii-chan.

00:18:37.790 --> 00:18:40.690
Here, it's your favorite, Gekiganger.

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:43.180
I won't make fun of you anymore, so please hang on!

00:18:44.270 --> 00:18:45.730
Okay, Yukina.

00:18:46.630 --> 00:18:48.860
Minato-san, take this...

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:58.400
Shiratori-san...

00:19:00.790 --> 00:19:01.490
Tenkawa-kun...

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:06.010
Too bad, we won't be able to watch the last episode together.

00:19:09.220 --> 00:19:12.290
Never forget the heart within you that believes in justice.

00:19:19.950 --> 00:19:21.170
Onii-chan?!

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:25.820
No!

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:42.290
Shiratori Tsukumo was a spy from Earth.

00:19:42.960 --> 00:19:44.160
You need not concern yourself.

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:49.830
His death will be reported to our people as an act perpetuated by Earth.

00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:53.250
The blame for the breakdown in peace negotiations will be attributed to them as well.

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:57.860
All the doves on our home world will undoubtedly lose power.

00:19:58.290 --> 00:19:59.200
You did a fine job.

00:19:59.510 --> 00:19:59.900
Sir.

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:05.300
We finally have the city. I'll be damned if we sue for peace now.

00:20:06.030 --> 00:20:06.810
Damn!

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:08.720
Damn this!

00:20:11.180 --> 00:20:14.960
Damn...

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:20.270
I didn't see what was right in front of me.

00:20:21.620 --> 00:20:24.580
Because I liked it, because I liked it so much,

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:27.290
I only saw the parts that made sense to me.

00:20:35.050 --> 00:20:35.840
Akito...

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:47.370
A real roller-coaster ride! The Gordian knot untied!

00:21:47.370 --> 00:21:49.490
Thank you for our high popularity! May the Force be with you!

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:51.200
Only two more episodes to go in Martian Successor Nadesico,

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:53.580
which you have supported so generously!

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:56.200
With everyone's love, hope, and emotions on board,

00:21:56.200 --> 00:21:58.310
we set sail to Mars, the land where all the mysteries sleep quietly.

00:21:58.310 --> 00:22:00.910
Behold the excitement you'll feel as you watch our dear Nadesico

00:22:00.910 --> 00:22:03.320
venture against the evil Jovian Federation and United Earth.

00:22:03.320 --> 00:22:05.470
We'll make your cry and laugh to the very end!

00:22:05.470 --> 00:22:07.440
The next Martian Successor Nadesico:

00:22:07.440 --> 00:22:09.400
"Being Myself, Being Yourself!"

00:22:09.400 --> 00:22:11.160
Let's watch it, everyone!
